[parity] Faithful native port of ChargerSpecsPanel.tsx: GlassPanel + section title "Charger Specs Breakdown"
(lucide Gauge → SF gauge glyph, neon-purple → chartSeriesPower token); the four SpecColumns in source order —
By Voltage (Zap→bolt.fill), By Phase (Activity→waveform.path.ecg), By Cable (Cable→cable.connector),
By Brand (Plug→powerplug.fill, showAvgPower); each row "{count} sessions · {metric}" where the Brand column shows
`${fmtInt(avgPower)} kW avg` when a power reading exists else `fmtWithUnit(energy,'kWh')`, and every other column
shows energy; each column renders its own empty message when its items are empty; and the panel `hasData` gate
(voltage||cable||brand — Phase deliberately excluded, exactly as the web source). SI is read at the boundary:
energy arrives in watt-hours, power in watts, converted to kWh/kW only at projection (lib/unitConversion.ts
parity). Adds the native query lifecycle the web parent owns: loading skeleton grid, QueryError-style retry,
stale freshness chip + once-per-episode auto-refresh, offline cached banner. All 10 web i18n keys
